#: ../../../cmds/return.rst:2
msgid "return - stop the current inner function"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cmds/return.rst:5
msgid "Synopsis"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cmds/return.rst:7
msgid "return [N]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cmds/return.rst:12
msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cmds/return.rst:14
msgid ":program:`return` halts a currently running function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cmds/return.rst:16
msgid ""
"It is often added inside of a conditional block such as an :doc:`if <if>` "
"statement or a :doc:`switch <switch>` statement to conditionally stop the "
"executing function and return to the caller; it can also be used to specify "
"the exit status of a function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cmds/return.rst:18
msgid ""
"If invoked outside of a function by a non-interactive shell, or inside :doc:"
"`source <source>`, it is equivalent to :doc:`exit <exit>`, meaning it it "
"will stop execution of the current script."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cmds/return.rst:20
msgid ""
"If invoked outside of a function by an interactive shell shell, execution "
"will continue as normal."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cmds/return.rst:22
msgid "The **-h** or **--help** option displays help about using this command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cmds/return.rst:25
msgid "Exit status"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cmds/return.rst:27
msgid "*N* if given, the previous exit status (:envvar:`status`) otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cmds/return.rst:30
msgid "Example"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cmds/return.rst:32
msgid "An implementation of the false command as a fish function: ::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cmds/return.rst:35
msgid ""
"function false\n"
"    return 1\n"
"end"
msgstr ""
